drawably (https://github.com/danielwh2/drawably), MIT License.
The hand-drawn pen stroke and boil in runtime/kit/rough.js re-implement its approach: points
sampled along a shape, jittered by a seeded stream, smoothed through their midpoints with quadratic
curves and drawn twice with a wilder second pass; the boil is three frames that add a small second
jitter over one shared base. The code is rewritten in our own ES modules with a fixed sampling plan
per box, so a sketch can morph and straighten, and the frame comes from the kit's time, not a CSS
clock. patterns/transitions/sketch-to-ink takes the idea of handing each piece over as the pen closes
it; no code is taken from the upstream films.

