Rewritten in JavaScript (not copied) in scripts/lib/sound-place.mjs, scripts/lib/sound-mix.mjs,
scripts/lib/sound-audible.mjs, scripts/lib/beat-kick.mjs and scripts/check/W-AUDIBLE.mjs: the way its
real-sound mixer aligns a sound by attack, peak or end measured on the sound, its QA's sync, audibility and
harshness measures, the provenance trace of every add, the flux search that puts a beat grid on the measured
attacks, and the traps of its level model. No audio, model, measurement of third-party films or realness
scorer is taken.

scripts/lib/sound-ab.mjs rewrites the fairness steps of its blind-test builder in JavaScript: both
sounds trimmed at one decay level with a 4 ms fade-in, matched on the K-weighted loudest 100 ms or 400 ms
by one common gain that keeps the true peak at -1 dBTP or under, the limits that refuse a pair, the
randomised sides with the first sound on exactly half of the trials and the one-sided binomial score.
No code, sound or model of the upstream project is shipped beyond that.

Ported into JavaScript, in our own idiom, from the model-free parts of its sound forge: the 28-band
third-octave profile and the third-octave x 10 ms bandgram (scripts/lib/audio-measure.mjs), the
bed-subtracted measurement of an event and its decay-shape and stutter reading, the damped-sinusoid
(ESPRIT) modal fit with its least-squares amplitudes (scripts/lib/modal-fit.mjs, with the small
linear algebra in scripts/lib/linalg.mjs), the fit-quality score (a multi-resolution log-mel, an
envelope correlation, an onset sharpness, a tone distance and excess and missing energy over
third-octave x 10 ms cells: scripts/lib/sound-score.mjs), the evolution strategy with its model-free
prescreen (scripts/lib/sound-search.mjs) and the artifact detectors (clicks, DC, clipping, a
truncated tail, a comb ring, a tail that rises again, stacked attacks, the rising glide:
scripts/lib/sound-artifacts.mjs). None of its models, trained weights, measurements or audio is
used.

Re-implemented in our own JavaScript in runtime/kit/synth.js, runtime/kit/modes.js and runtime/kit/aim.js, and
in the recipes under patterns/sound/ (whoosh, downlifter, pop-in, key, counter, ding, click, sub-drop, cut-hit,
