The retry and refusal rules in scripts/lib/http.mjs are restated in our own JavaScript from its SDK client
and its provider-refusal classifier: a 429 or a 5xx retried twice, Retry-After honoured up to 30 s, a
250 x 2^n ms backoff, one idempotency key for each POST and its retries, and a refusal sorted into
the key being refused, the account being out of credit or the rate limit being reached, from the status
and the first words of the body, with the body never printed. No other code is taken.

